{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_01faf88b050a3d2b0c0242022942d26503004c107c7f306f5264b4f1509826f4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3ba78b2b643299cc317924e81de88e7a77cf29d16efedbf3f85d37df7f75d8a4","slc_7a413246163358625b3bcc2d30cc16327c2c92706a2c021701e8aad3abf00f90","slc_f5dacd6afab0f0852f3dd3cf56fb991188b37d04fb7d6a944fcd0214d39e1dab"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"MCP servers run as child processes over stdio, registered via smelt.mcp.register with command, args, env, timeout (default 30000ms) and enabled fields; only the local server kind is supported.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_08ff060ee9a569accd2a6d45cb983231814d8a2524588a52571ac7f6d7d164b3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_56062ee10d20402f8a119cf5325c8f9d5a6c63e619ced4637c2d306241a06664","slc_a2fb730d8d30db7eadd4d57cb0a8bf90b9e0275b2c10046fb547f44131d27828"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Skills are on-demand knowledge packs loaded via the load_skill tool, scanned from global and project-local smelt, Claude-compatible (~/.claude, .claude), and Agent Skills-compatible (~/.agents, .agents) directories, with later entries overriding earlier ones.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1f7bbd6ee1d170a4b81c8c3b1e3fde70a8500979f80a0109ba1c84eca654e566","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_097d93de3e97b3255536e5abb0d4b085e91f7f9e5641ee1dda70aa474028c8d8"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"The reload guarantee covers only smelt-owned declarations; Lua config is trusted in-process code, not a sandbox, so arbitrary filesystem, process, or network side effects of a failing candidate are not rolled back.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_23ec5129778e3078951204d7d3ef4a105c6b4b2b3ac1d99b19a7efb7cfbb3ab8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_99e1a8c60d89cb471d7c88f377e9461ff8415a05fcb42dc1b80986d03e796f6a","slc_cd3e56ccf427454601ebd5cae8d52f1f1a56a1c8108df92720dfde1db02ab546"],"source_ids":["src_5fba37715dec57a3970e0654d6cf6105"],"text":"The product includes Lua plugins (keymaps, commands, autocmds, custom tools, custom modes), a self-built terminal grid/layout renderer, a vim-style editor with motions, text objects, registers and undo, and deterministic fuzzing with a fixed clock and stubbed I/O so crashes can be replayed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3109c3ca64c4a93d8fd555ba21e0e8de5862549b0e9578eb71c28b07097935db","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8952bc3ff3c882fc7431f6b8727e541362a49580f661994309653c2398777bb2"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Themes are ThemeSpec Lua tables with a required groups table keyed by highlight-group names; built-in colorschemes live in runtime/lua/smelt/colorschemes/ and custom ones drop into the user config directory, loaded via smelt.theme.use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3fc1d190502cc98b3833c79e1e0f7664afec16b3415f6e2d55c99435c6b2cb44","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4d4eb737679b198adffafa40592511dfe94f22845492968836661cb14a6aa77c","slc_8a59acccc3db10c138f278e3b96dcf8e2965153d697fce96afb2dc2982951dc3","slc_8f739ebfad8e2c14c6e18283c080cbca76d4b4537d14955c54aaaa3b89b114ef","slc_927108691b824e2744d7fde2ac4893421a9ee495fde560c59574f1a62ff52790"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"smelt uses four platform directories (config, state, data, cache) under XDG bases on Linux/macOS, storing sessions databases, OAuth credential files, recent.json picks, per-workspace permissions, prompt history, trust hashes, rotated logs, and a read-only mirror of the embedded Lua runtime.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_42bb5d43ada0617fcf111a5d7a4d308506224d9f1127c50fee6486bed7f3e584","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4859da3ab8828d60e6973106a04565a67fea6c7a82d86bf1152b600fad89801e","slc_677e8e6e52eb3e9b0a714d41bcf10966b5526f64a837bb61565f01190063769d","slc_d88fbe49200eef805853b249cfb4a2d8222e19f1f8cc7856219f3258c10e8c26"],"source_ids":["src_5fba37715dec57a3970e0654d6cf6105"],"text":"API-key providers are configured with `--model`, `--api-base`, and `--api-key-env`, supporting any OpenAI-compatible endpoint such as a local Ollama server or OpenAI/Anthropic/OpenRouter.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_47accdd61b9129ca1481c8ce92e68259b2a051f44884572e63ef59a8a73aff5c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2e3597a3efe41bc93badd8bddb311c6554ddf347f88d7d4d5d2907960edf87b1","slc_72caed92c0e7b60dbf7cca26e34ae5c79b79e44cb62f2c29b7301b3fc9ecdc76"],"source_ids":["src_5fba37715dec57a3970e0654d6cf6105"],"text":"smelt is described as beta software until 1.0, released with normal 0.x.y versions rather than SemVer prereleases, and interfaces may still change between releases.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4f8b31aca3635118f023e0608c75ad65127ab4e6c2f6f4a5aed2d0a5d891209d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_135612f0d0f3c3e6c63b40c440b586db0578f743a03efb03c632f047a0a39e70"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"smelt-managed configuration reloads transactionally: a fresh candidate is validated before replacing the running generation, and on failure existing commands, keymaps, tools, hooks, providers, settings, permissions, MCP/LSP declarations and watcher roots stay active.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_552e8b273512f2b526a41c0e8e59e7b5a998e26680434966cfa398a82079ea1e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_028f30d2cad522024a66270491e5e54e08023e8e1787600e3bcf15fb86eaaef0","slc_ce3cd5ae04233bbd8089201659d30f2032fe33df2412bea35393364e9881dbbd","slc_f9b6aac5b3b280e7ccc394afb7487483805b82face45b77020d790d350fc2a6d"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Model resolution on fresh launch follows CLI --model, then last explicitly chosen model from recent.json, then smelt.defaults.set in init.lua, then the first picker-visible model; /model switches at runtime and the choice is restored next launch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5556b9a585bed1aeb0f9bfd7e2fe94b2291a09f01567b61b11d4acda95d86c6f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d43b3b13192b8393de1a6c626b23eedf1ee4f06ea3f3ee606778a3501ba1e274"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Fast mode requests accelerated inference but requires the active model to resolve supports_fast_mode=true; /fast on|off|toggle changes the session and unsupported models reject the command.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_568bd025fee07da25be82a6580745c4f3127ed434593d51406016b8c0647b1cc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1258cf5f862683710310c7fe9e06f4e0415fe00976eb2b9bce75a5d06265344a","slc_4216b0bb6da678e570954a96d06f8f7abffbda5383d6c4ec55630330c307b103","slc_8069a13c0ae2ebac661768582bdc20deeee25034a068f478e66bc58f7303c56c","slc_d59d9c43155d2d0ee0f9dabab38a4a0331034f50d83965f05c4ae003e20e0765","slc_fbefb510d87594dd6053840518d5b0e5622b85055210208c328d264310d9c0dc"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Each skill is a directory containing a SKILL.md with YAML frontmatter (name, description) followed by agent instructions, and may include reference assets.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_655ec79d3a4400355f00bb82c67b0ecf8bfd93d4af195c47bf7d2e3dbcb48b57","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_491376a940032a039339da14fd8aa2b49d725eff281d97e113574979a2529d16","slc_a4aa9bb6d59f70fc05db3de0a0e9740cbfe60b5cd461cd87c5700366b357961e","slc_c9059de6e582d7596419e502610f43b762856986acdc9afbb14515b2ff4b1102","slc_d8350cf61bef17a03a0eb2882e44f9457994eabca09b136c9e36c49ed07e338b"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Settings are written to smelt.settings in init.lua or via --set KEY=VALUE; unknown keys raise at access and type mismatches on assignment, and settings apply to the running session without writing to disk themselves.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_66a78b864f25d3c1cd27c47bb99e942d70e47a7e2ea125985d5ece1345a6a2bb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2da43436ce787fb37d39f051429acb555eae08c1b89cc806886ee00e23d66050","slc_5c330c1ed66cad335bceea86122f1e304cd5e9ad390eb63a9a53aaf2049f5c43","slc_a20b545139af4e79804d87259604a61bf8df94425a76e984c993af18ed5933df"],"source_ids":["src_5fba37715dec57a3970e0654d6cf6105"],"text":"The project is MIT-licensed and states it is inspired by Claude Code and Neovim, with documentation hosted at leonardcser.github.io/smelt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b938d252a89c0e7724b7d387006abe74a5c809ae22ec775666dab0412622d58","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1aeb771114c7970d2205c71136aa275b7bb65590b9f14f005ffbf46fd2d1e2cf","slc_4e143f033632702870bac43833e4fa6b145a24d4cb7a437e2746f09dfdde9c2c"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"MCP tools appear in the agent's tool list with server-prefixed names (e.g. filesystem_read_file), default to ask permission, and are governed by a separate mcp ruleset matching qualified tool names.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e03e157fdbc6c013c0a3ee48aa43097945ec6a38b63ec958870d0c1dd449b38","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_55f7414f3fad5fad5da7d906a3d0c6590863f3a39a3887aa591a719f81c32f43","slc_94654f5aaff2f82b0b6dd713573045f407713f2f5c93a56aa47307ba6ed7f19b","slc_d704bf6eac72822b74ef4caea391de90a0f68fae4f4880df0520e1bd20ffda83"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Modes and reasoning effort are set via CLI flags or init.lua and toggled at runtime with Shift+Tab (modes) and Ctrl+T (reasoning); reasoning levels include off/low/medium/high/xhigh/max/ultra plus provider-defined labels.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7457678b021cf6a302a341ebdc5f63a89a2662cd3733d096f85ca9519b2f1513","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_857026058ae931aec34df05f89568980a6e117b04d23ebd7324cd29650d28680"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Provider types map to specific endpoints, e.g. openai-compatible to /v1/chat/completions (Ollama, vLLM, llama.cpp, Gemini), openai to /v1/responses, anthropic to /v1/messages with thinking, and OAuth-backed codex/copilot/kimi-code endpoints.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b04a9dda990acbafeabb1b09779a2d87ca4d2640caec14b27b4d7e6f020bca3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_941cd853e0548d279ece929c57a9d5e38ea6f48b491bfef675ce5f07d51c9fc2","slc_b6eb1a7b53819755edcced3b8328fe60470a12802b820bdf36e75efb998092d5","slc_bccbec4e43de3ca84c30d17146f457dc253bc53eb27f84f734d51e09e6f4efff"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"The request_audit setting controls provider-request records stored per session database: summary metadata by default, full reconstructable payloads, or off; SMELT_REQUEST_AUDIT pins the mode per process and overrides Lua config even after /reload.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7b623d545e312f30a9140e283103929f349e8921b1f50c460a09b49aa9363e73","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7a4d2daa068ad59a9891136c8834bb63745ff3dad96071555181d900ee163141","slc_b2b71b29e9ed7ad635a243315b2189943a5a2736ea6de2a54257d5073b3d2a32","slc_ba7e37286614f8e851f8a165359c55c43ac86d7bc1e8597751d4c970bdf29034"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32","src_e26d951cba7258bda00b31b8e206ddcc"],"text":"Per-model overrides cover sampling (temperature, top_p, top_k, min_p, repeat_penalty), tool_calling toggle, context window, reasoning/fast-mode support, thinking budgets, and USD-per-1M-token cost fields.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_81a88d1b1245837f64db73ca7c9167bd388de896d3bff97986bb7b4967a6e951","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_18fc0035916c0368a35ac7440b036dc1ab39b0a26d223c0f3b4c349dce76a37b","slc_951daf016af1bcfb498a1e0d26f6d456ce4ed58afb3ae178a2530b86f6355a71"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"Cost tracking is built in for popular models like GPT, Claude, and DeepSeek; subscription-backed providers show zero cost, session cost appears in the status bar, totals in /stats, and unknown models default to zero cost.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_824f2a058b3741e4db0a62d37a1bc26776b57e3232fc339d8940fb799e9072fc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_26f11a9a961e58d0e29e9ce992eeb62724dc984d2818e6125ffc99db47cbc0d3","slc_3d225980d5296c623bac0230e6e0c2b5479dce9763aaccebe5120df1040583c2"],"source_ids":["src_5fba37715dec57a3970e0654d6cf6105"],"text":"smelt is installable from source with cargo install --locked from its GitHub repository, and prebuilt binaries are offered for Linux and macOS (x86_64, aarch64) plus Windows x86_64.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_85daeb1c3425a6e917ee6a7752919d8606cfcc239f83a143a414b5d087ba2c32","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_177fcfc9e036b7f08ccd25e157edf3a8e33a05f62f62a3a5677cf7435ef47794"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"OAuth credentials load from a provider-specific environment override, then a private JSON file in the state directory, then the OS keyring; smelt auth writes both file and keyring storage with 0600 files on Unix, and logout removes both copies.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","created_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8fb71e1117d6e844a74b0e4725ae384ec7d00283985e50b12403b0e84be0df24","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"leonardcser/smelt@9a7e6536df52 snapshot 1b7df65587b36aa1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f625dfd241bae3ff6f119c6e0b82819ac329ae4240103e31bf44f7287a9a128","slc_9a1b770a1323ac0c1a64d4de0a66a59c66e13369ab27fcd7e50bc269ade51029"],"source_ids":["src_537cc59157de59569296c20660b40a32"],"text":"On quota or rate-limit errors the conversation pauses with queued messages held; retries back off from 1 to 2, 4, then every 5 minutes, honoring provider reset times, and manual retry is done by pressing Enter with an empty prompt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:12:19Z","updated_by_operation":"op_5f444d500a594b6db8f54be079140636"}
